P&L: payment provider fees in SG&A

Sales are booked gross, so what Nexi, PayPal and Amex take has to show
as a cost or the margin reads better than it was.

The three charge in three different ways, so the line cannot come from
the bills. Nexi invoices monthly and debits the account; its fee is
taken from the period it covers, not the day it left, so August's fee
sits in August. PayPal and Amex keep theirs out of the payout and never
invoice at all, so theirs is read off the monthly statement.

A guard keeps a forwarded provider bill out of the other SG&A lines -
counted twice is worse than not counted - and the fold-out lists the
providers rather than claiming there are no bills.

September shows PayPal's 207,45 alone until the Nexi statement and an
Amex overview are filed. Nexi holds July (1.334,89) and August
(1.256,24) only.

